RUNG 10 — find: meaningful paths, found automatically
  From a string to every string said to be a word, by the shortest readings that keep
  their meaning. No walking by hand, no scores. `find tomas ip` is the ip of tomas.

  usage:  find tomas ip FILE.eoe ...                the ip of tomas
          find dana ip FILE.eoe ...                 two hops: dana's order came from web-01.corp
          find bob ip --slack=1 FILE.eoe ...        none clean; the nearest with one weak link
          find bob ip --loose FILE.eoe ...          no limit on broken rules
          --hops=N   give up after N hops (4)

a hop = up to a whole, down to another part of it       (things meet only through a whole)
words are never walked; they only name the lines

rules that keep a reading meaningful:
    kept       a string passed through is the same word coming in and going out
               (10.2.14.7 is ip in the login and ip in hosts: a join;
                "1" is seq in one and quantity in the other: a coincidence)
    distinct   no two wholes of the same kind in one reading
               (login → "Accepted" → another login: shared value, not shared thing)

find within(start, target, slack):
    readings = [just the start]
    for hop count 1 .. --hops:
        for each reading, each whole of its last string:
            breaks = rules this hop would break
            skip if the reading's breaks + these > slack
            for each other part of the whole:
                extend the reading with this hop (and its breaks)
                if the part is said to be target:  it's an answer
        if any answers:  return all of them       (ties are different explanations)
    return none

find(start, target):
    for slack = 0, 1, ... up to --slack (0):      (--loose: no limit)
        answers = find within(start, target, slack)
        if answers:  return them, and the slack they took
    return none

print each answer once, its readings under it, each hop as
    "<words> in <kind> <whole> → <words> <part>"
with any break shown above its hop:  ⚠ "1" is seq on the way in, quantity on the way out
